{
  "name": "groups-roles",
  "steps": [
    {
      "note": "revision 12: the wire-group surface renders EXPORTED Straza roles (id = role id, displayName = role name). The IdM discovers them by the displayName filter, exactly how group linking works in the wild.",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups?filter=displayName eq \"scim-dev\""
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "subset": {
          "totalResults": 1,
          "Resources": [
            {
              "displayName": "scim-dev"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "creating access is Straza's act, never the IdM's: POST answers 501 (RFC 7644 unsupported operation; NOT 403, which IdM runbooks read as broken credentials), with the doctrine spoken in detail.",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups",
        "body": {
          "schemas": [
            "urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:Group"
          ],
          "displayName": "idm-born-team"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 501,
        "subset": {
          "detail": "roles are born in Straza, so the IdM cannot create or delete one over SCIM. Create the role in Straza, import it as a group, and assign membership from the IdM"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "a user to hold the role",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Users",
        "body": {
          "schemas": [
            "urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:User"
          ],
          "userName": "wanda"
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 201,
        "subset": {
          "userName": "wanda"
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "uid": "id"
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "membership IS role assignment: a members add creates the direct scim-origin assignment and the render reflects it",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups?filter=displayName eq \"scim-dev\""
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200
      },
      "capture": {
        "gid": "Resources.0.id"
      }
    },
    {
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups/{gid}",
        "body": {
          "schemas": [
            "urn:ietf:params:scim:api:messages:2.0:PatchOp"
          ],
          "Operations": [
            {
              "op": "add",
              "path": "members",
              "value": [
                {
                  "value": "{uid}"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "subset": {
          "members": [
            {
              "value": "{uid}"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "renaming access is Straza's act too: displayName is readOnly and an explicit PATCH answers the mutability error",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups/{gid}",
        "body": {
          "schemas": [
            "urn:ietf:params:scim:api:messages:2.0:PatchOp"
          ],
          "Operations": [
            {
              "op": "replace",
              "path": "displayName",
              "value": "renamed"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 400,
        "subset": {
          "schemas": [
            "urn:ietf:params:scim:api:messages:2.0:Error"
          ],
          "scimType": "mutability"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "PUT is a TOLERANT members replace: the name fields in the body are ignored (Okta sends the full document, displayName included, on every membership update) and the response re-renders server truth",
      "request": {
        "method": "PUT",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups/{gid}",
        "body": {
          "schemas": [
            "urn:ietf:params:scim:schemas:core:2.0:Group"
          ],
          "displayName": "Okta Developers",
          "members": [
            {
              "value": "{uid}"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "subset": {
          "displayName": "scim-dev",
          "members": [
            {
              "value": "{uid}"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "value-filter remove converges membership off again",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups/{gid}",
        "body": {
          "schemas": [
            "urn:ietf:params:scim:api:messages:2.0:PatchOp"
          ],
          "Operations": [
            {
              "op": "remove",
              "path": "members[value eq \"{uid}\"]"
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "subset": {
          "displayName": "scim-dev"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "deleting access is Straza's act: DELETE answers 501 like create",
      "request": {
        "method": "DELETE",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups/{gid}"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 501,
        "subset": {
          "detail": "roles are born in Straza, so the IdM cannot create or delete one over SCIM. Create the role in Straza, import it as a group, and assign membership from the IdM"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "revision 19: a server-owned role is a wire-group like any other, found by the displayName filter and carrying the owning server under server; the reference server's seed created scim-tools-readers on scim-tools [doc: derived from the reference server's TestSCIMGroupProjectionServer, not captured from a live wire]",
      "request": {
        "method": "GET",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups?filter=displayName eq \"scim-tools-readers\""
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "subset": {
          "totalResults": 1,
          "Resources": [
            {
              "displayName": "scim-tools-readers",
              "urn:straza:params:scim:schemas:extension:2.0:Group": {
                "server": "scim-tools"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "capture": {
        "sgid": "Resources.0.id"
      }
    },
    {
      "note": "revision 19: membership on a server-owned wire-group is the identity manager's as on every other, so a members add creates the direct scim-origin assignment and the render keeps naming the owning server",
      "request": {
        "method": "PATCH",
        "path": "/scim/v2/Groups/{sgid}",
        "body": {
          "schemas": [
            "urn:ietf:params:scim:api:messages:2.0:PatchOp"
          ],
          "Operations": [
            {
              "op": "add",
              "path": "members",
              "value": [
                {
                  "value": "{uid}"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": 200,
        "subset": {
          "displayName": "scim-tools-readers",
          "members": [
            {
              "value": "{uid}"
            }
          ],
          "urn:straza:params:scim:schemas:extension:2.0:Group": {
            "server": "scim-tools"
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
